---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const open = `const lease = await db.records.open({ path: "notes/today.md" }, {
  autosave: { idleMs: 1_000 }, // leave out for explicit flush() only
});
const { session } = lease;

const unsubscribe = session.subscribe(() => render(session.getSnapshot()));
editor.onChange((text) => session.setBody(text));
properties.onChange((patch) => session.patchFrontmatter(patch)); // undefined unsets a key`;

const leave = `const result = await session.flush({ timeoutMs: 8_000 });
if (!result.ok) {
  const snapshot = session.getSnapshot();
  if (snapshot.state === "conflict") {
    showConflict(snapshot.body, snapshot.remote); // your text and the newer record
  } else {
    showProblem(result.problem);
  }
}
unsubscribe();
lease.release();`;

const resolve = `session.resolve({ keep: "mine" });   // put your changes on top of the newer record
session.resolve({ keep: "theirs" }); // take the newer record
session.resolve({ body: merged });   // save text the user merged`;

const recover = `// Keep this with your own saved state, for example in IndexedDB.
const recovery = session.getSnapshot().recovery;
if (recovery) {
  saveRecovery({
    mutationId: recovery.mutationId,
    recordId: recovery.recordId,
    baseRevision: recovery.baseRevision,
  });
}

// After a reload:
const lease = await db.records.open(recordId, { recovery: loadRecovery() });`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Editing records"
  description="Keep one record open while people type: autosave, conflicts, lost responses and deletions handled by one shared session."
  active="editing"
  headings={[
    { href: "#open", label: "Open a record" },
    { href: "#follow", label: "Stay current" },
    { href: "#states", label: "States" },
    { href: "#conflicts", label: "Conflicts" },
    { href: "#leave", label: "Leave safely" },
    { href: "#custom", label: "Survive a reload" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    An app that lets people type into a record should not call
    {" "}<code>update()</code> on every keystroke. Open the record as a session
    instead. The session saves after a pause in typing, never runs two saves
    for the same record at once, and tells your interface what state the
    record is in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="open">Open a record</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={open} language="ts" label="editor.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>db.records.open()</code> takes an ID, a <code>&#123; path &#125;</code>
    {" "}or a record you read. It returns a lease: the <code>session</code> and
    a <code>release()</code> function for this view. Every view that opens the
    same record on the same client shares one session, so your app never has
    two competing writers for it. Views that share a session must use the same
    autosave setting.
  </p>
  <p>
    The lease is local to your app. It does not lock the record for anyone
    else.
  </p>

  <h2 id="follow">Stay current while it is open</h2>
  <p>
    An open session follows the collection’s change feed. When the record
    changes elsewhere, the session reads it again. Without local changes, it
    shows the newer record. With local changes, it moves to
    {" "}<code>conflict</code> and keeps both: your text, and the newer record
    in <code>snapshot.remote</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="states">States</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>saved</code>: the text is the record, confirmed by the log.</li>
    <li><code>saved_on_device</code>: the text is kept on this device and syncs when the log can be reached.</li>
    <li><code>unsaved</code>: local changes wait for autosave or <code>flush()</code>.</li>
    <li><code>saving</code>: a save is in flight. Typing continues; newer text is saved next.</li>
    <li><code>conflict</code>: the record changed elsewhere while you had unsaved changes, or it is held.</li>
    <li>
      <code>recovery</code>: a save’s outcome is not known yet. The session
      waits for that save’s own receipt and never sends a replacement.
    </li>
    <li><code>error</code>: the last save failed. Your text is kept.</li>
    <li><code>deleted</code>: the record no longer exists. Your text is kept.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <code>snapshot.problem</code> holds the error behind <code>error</code>
    {" "}and <code>recovery</code>. <code>snapshot.dirty</code> tells you
    whether there are unsaved changes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="conflicts">Conflicts</h2>
  <p>
    Each save also checks the revision your text was based on, so a change
    the session hasn’t seen yet still can’t be overwritten. In
    {" "}<code>conflict</code>, let the user choose:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={resolve} language="ts" label="conflict.ts" />
  <p>
    A session can’t resolve a <a href="/sdk/offline-sync/#holds">hold</a>.
    Held records stay protected until the user resolves the hold itself.
  </p>

  <h2 id="leave">Leave safely</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={leave} language="ts" label="leave.ts" />
  <p>
    <code>flush()</code> resolves once there is nothing left to save and the
    log has confirmed it, or tells you why it can’t. If the change is kept on
    this device but not confirmed yet, it resolves with <code>ok: true</code>
    {" "}and <code>saved: "on_device"</code>. Releasing the last view
    stops autosave but keeps unsaved text, so opening the record again on the
    same client picks it up. A client keeps at most 64 sessions with unsaved
    text; settle some before opening more.
  </p>

  <h2 id="custom">Survive a reload</h2>
  <p>
    Unsaved text lives in memory. If a save was sent but its outcome is not
    yet known when the page reloads, keep the session’s recovery reference and
    pass it back to <code>open()</code>. The session then finishes that same
    save instead of writing again.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={recover} language="ts" label="recover.ts" />
</DocsLayout>
